-- title:
--   Lifting a 1-critical η₁-section through Pi
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative ring of characteristic $p$, and $j\colon \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to B$ a ring homomorphism; let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$, that is, a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ over $B$ together with an action of $\mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ by formal group endomorphisms and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$. Write $M$ for the Cartier module of $X.F$ and, for $n$, let $M_n$ be the subgroup of those $f$ with $a_c \cdot f = j(\tau(c))^{p^n} f$ for all $c \in \mathbb{F}_{p^2}$, where $a_c$ is the action of the Teichmüller lift $\tau(c)$ and the right-hand side is the homothety. Assume $M_0$ and $M_1$ are complementary ($hc$), and let $D$ be the resulting graded Cartier module datum, with $\Pi$ given by $\varpi$, $V$ by the integral Verschiebung, $N(M) = D.\mathrm{NMod}$ the quotient of $M \times M^{(\sigma)}$ by the relations generated by $(Vm, -\Pi m)$, $\lambda(\!(m,m')\!) = \Pi m + V m'$, $\Pi_N(\!(m,m')\!) = (\!(\Pi m, \Pi m')\!)$ and $u\colon N(M) \to M/VM$ the map induced by the first projection. Let $L\colon M \to N(M)$ be an additive map which is a canonical $L$-map: it is $\sigma$-semilinear, satisfies $L(Vx) = (\!(\Pi x,0)\!)$ and $\lambda \circ L = F$, and it is obtained by base change along a surjection from a Cartier $L$-map on a special graded Cartier module over a ring with no $p$-torsion. Write $\eta_i(L)$ for `etaPiece`, the intersection of the subgroup `eta L` of $N(M)$ with the image under $(\!(\cdot,\cdot)\!)$ of $M_i \times M_i$. Assume the explicit description $\eta_1(L) = \{(\!(m,0)\!) : m \in M_1,\ \Pi m = Vm\}$ ($hEta1$), and assume that every $m \in M_1$ with $\Pi m = Vm$ which lies in $\Pi M_0 + VM$ is of the form $\lambda(z_0)$ for some $z_0 \in \eta_0(L)$ ($hlift$). Then for every $z \in \eta_1(L)$ whose image under $u$ is the class of $\Pi m_0$ modulo $VM$ for some $m_0 \in M_0$, there is $z_0 \in \eta_0(L)$ with $\Pi_N(z_0) = z$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity step of Drinfeld's criticality condition [C2] at an index-$1$ critical point, in the form used by Boutot and Carayol in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: a section of $\eta_1(L)$ whose tangent class comes from $\Pi M_0$ is $\Pi_N$ of a section of $\eta_0(L)$. It is the mirror image, with the two graded pieces exchanged, of the corresponding statement at an index-$0$ critical point, and it feeds the argument over an algebraically closed base (`exists_nVarpi_eq_of_mem_etaPiece_of_toLieQuot_eq_of_isAlgClosed`).
